{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-129937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,2].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-129937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(\\frac{1}{4+{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot [\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-(-1-1)\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{8}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-129937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-129937" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-129937" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{8}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-129937" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-71932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{ }{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[0,\\pi ]\\times [0,1].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-71932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{ }{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\text{ }({e}^{y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi }\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)\\cdot ({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-(-1-1)\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =2(e-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-71932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-71932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-71932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2e"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2(1-e)"] ["math" "2(e-1)"] ["math" "2e"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-71932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2(e-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{y}}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,\\sqrt{3}]\\times [0,1].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{{e}^{y}}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}})({e}^{y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot [{e}^{y}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1)\\cdot ({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}(e-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-80511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{12}(1-e)"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{12}(e-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}(e-1)"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}(1-e)"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}(e-1)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{12}(e-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})(\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\operatorname{sin}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =(1-0)\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-80507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-129936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}+1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A$ over the rectangle $R=[1,e]\\times [0,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-129936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{{y}^{2}+1}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{1}{x})({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}({y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{1}^{e}\\cdot [\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\cdot (\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+3) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-129936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-129936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-129936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "12e"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6e"] ["math" "e+6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-129936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${∬}_{R}(6{x}^{2}-10{y}^{4})\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[-2,0]\\times [-1,1].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(6{x}^{2}-10{y}^{4})\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}6{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}10{y}^{4}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}6{x}^{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(1-(-1)){\\int }_{-2}^{0}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2{x}^{3}{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot {0}^{3}-2\\cdot (-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}10{y}^{4}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(0-(-2)){\\int }_{-1}^{1}10{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2{y}^{5}{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot {1}^{5}-2\\cdot (-1)^{5}) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(6{x}^{2}+10{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}A=32-8=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-80638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-28"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "30"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80638" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-81243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,2]\\times [1,e].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-81243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{3}{y}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{3}{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}4{x}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3}{y}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-1){\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{3}{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|]_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}4{x}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(e-1){\\int }_{1}^{2}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(e-1)[{x}^{4}]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(e-1)({2}^{4}-{1}^{4}) \\\\  & =15(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{3-4y{x}^{3}}{y}\\,\\text{d}A=3-15(e-1)=18-15e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-81243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-81243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-81243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12-15e"] ["math" "15-12e"] ["math" "15e-18"] ["math" "18-15e"] ["math" "18e-15"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-81243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18-15e"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}\\frac{2+6y{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[1,2]\\times [2,4].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{2+6y{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+6y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{R}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}6y\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & =(4-2){\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{x}{|}_{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{2}-(-\\frac{2}{1})) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}6y\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(2-1){\\int }_{2}^{4}6y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =3({4}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}\\frac{2+6y{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A=2+36=38.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-80627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "18"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "26"] ["math" "38"] ["math" "48"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "38"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-81245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${∬}_{R}(4{y}^{3}-2x)\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[2,5]\\times [0,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-81245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(4{y}^{3}-2x)\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}4{y}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}2x\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}4{y}^{3}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(5-2){\\int }_{0}^{3}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3[{y}^{4}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3({3}^{4}-{0}^{4}) \\\\  & =243.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2x\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =(3-0){\\int }_{2}^{5}2x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3[{x}^{2}]_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =3({5}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =63.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(4{y}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}A=243-63=180.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-81245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-81245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-81245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "160"] ["math" "180"] ["math" "243"] ["math" "271"] ["math" "306"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-81245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "180"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A$,  where $R=[0,3]\\times [0,2].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{R}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the first integral is a constant, so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}A=2\\,\\text{Area}(R)=2\\cdot (3\\cdot 2)=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe function under the second integral is independent of $y.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}A & =(2-0){\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot [{x}^{2}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =2({3}^{2}-(0)^{2}) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function under the third integral is independent of $x.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}A & =(3-0){\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3\\cdot [{y}^{3}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =3({2}^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}(2+2x-3{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A=12+18-24=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-80626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\\frac{1}{2},\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\\frac{3}{2},\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{f(x,y)}{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}\\frac{f(x,y)}{2}\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-80661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80661" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/assets/939f859ef3454e31a9adaae7d72210ef670f93cbf3d77ecf87aa3879d8d0644c.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in S, \\\\ \\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}, & (x,y)\\in T, \\\\ \\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}, & (x,y)\\in U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}0\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{T}\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-80660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{∬}_{S}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{T}\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A"] ["math" "{∬}_{T\\cup U}\\frac{x+y}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A"] ["math" "{∬}_{T\\cup U}\\frac{x+y}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A"] ["math" "{∬}_{T}\\frac{x+y}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A"] ["math" "{∬}_{T}\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-80660" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{∬}_{T}\\frac{x}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{U}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-130020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=12,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-8,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-130020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =3{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =3(12-8) \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-130020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4268d8bae7a70f39a54b4e6287468d7ce3c5211a844a56c84c2509dc70d02393"} {"question" "q-130020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054242/state.json" "file_sha256" "7657dbc527d157b97356580289bf2db64fc387abe9b8da0e583ac2e0788f2e6b"} {"question" "q-130020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "