(U) notation denotes the same integration regions as the captured subscripts."}] "usage" {"q-80452" [] "e-7023" [] "q-71932" [] "e-6106" [] "e-6107" [] "e-6108" []} "basis" 1795 "retractions" [[17592186129782 :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $∬_(R)\\sin xe^{y}dA$ over the rectangle $R = [0, π] \\cdot [0, 1]$."] [17592186129810 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2000/Source/Images/q-80452.png)\n\nConsider the region $R$ shown above. Let the function $f(x, y)$ be defined as\n$f(x, y) = {x,\\begin{vmatrix}(x, y) ∈ S, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}(x, y) ∈ T,; x^{2}y, \\mid (x, y) ∈ U$.\nThen,\n$∬_(R)f(x, y)dA =$"] [17592186129810 :question/answer-fields 17592186128654] [17592186128924 :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} xy\\ \\!e^{x+y}\\ \\textrm d A$ over the rectangle $R= [0,1] \\times [1,2]$."] [17592186128924 :question/worked-solution "We apply the multiplicative property of double integrals and then evaluate each of the integrals separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\iint\\limits_{R} xy \\\\ e^{x+y}\\: \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R} \\Big(x\\ \\! e^x \\Big)\\Big(y\\ \\! e^{y} \\Big) \\textrm d A \\\\[5pt] &= \\left(\\int_0^1x \\\\ e^{x} \\ \\textrm d x\\right)\\left(\\int_1^2 y \\ \\!e^{y} \\ \\textrm d y\\right) \\\\[5pt] &= \\Big[x\\ \\!e^x-e^x\\Big]_0^1 \\cdot \\Big[y\\ \\!e^y-e^y\\Big]_1^2 \\\\[5pt] &= \\Big(e^1-e^1 - \\left(0-e^0\\right)\\Big) \\cdot \\Big(2e^2-e^2 - \\left(e^1-e^1\\right) \\Big) \\\\[5pt] &= 1\\cdot e^2 \\\\[5pt] &= e^2 \\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128925 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} \\left(x^2-y^2 +3\\right) \\textrm d A$, where $R= [-1,3] \\times [2, 4]$."] [17592186128925 :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity property of double integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(R)(x^{2} - y^{2} + 3)dA &= ∬_(R)x^{2}dA - ∬_(R)y^{2}dA + ∬_(R)3dA\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's evaluate each of the three integrals.\n\n- The function under the first integral is independent of $y$. So, we have\n$∬_(R)x^{2}dA|= (4 - 2)∫_{-1}^{3}x^{2}dx; = 2 \\cdot \\frac{x^{3}}{3} \\mid _{-1}^{3}; = 2(\\frac{27}{3} + \\frac{1}{3}); = \\frac{56}{3}$.\n- The function under the second integral is independent of $x$. So, we have\n$∬_(R)y^{2}dA|= (3 - (-1))∫_{2}^{4}y^{2}dy; = 4∫_{2}^{4}y^{2}dy; = 4 \\cdot \\frac{y^{3}}{3} \\mid _{2}^{4}; = \\frac{4}{3}4^{3} - \\frac{4}{3}2^{3}; = \\frac{224}{3}$.\n- The function under the third integral is a constant, so we have\n$∬_(R)3dA = 3Area(R) = 3 \\cdot (2 \\cdot 4) = 24$.\n\nFinally, combining our results, we obtain\n\n$$\n∬_(R)(x^{2} - y^{2} + 3)dA = \\frac{56}{3} - \\frac{224}{3} + 24 =-32\n$$"] [17592186128942 :question/problem "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n$\\iint\\limits_{C} f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = 8, \\qquad \\iint\\limits_{D} f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A = -5$,\nfind the value of\n$\\iint\\limits_{C \\cup D} 3f(x,y)\\ \\textrm{d}A$."] [17592186128942 :question/worked-solution "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(C∪D)3f(x, y)dA &= 3∬_(C∪D)f(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= 3(∬_(C)f(x, y)dA + ∬_(D)f(x, y)dA) \\\\\n&= 3(8 + (-5)) \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128926 :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{R} f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A$, where\n\n${2,\\begin{vmatrix}if0 < x < 2,-1 < y < 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{xy + x + y + 1},\\end{vmatrix}if0 < x < 2, 0 < y < 1$,\nand $R$ is the domain of $f$."] [17592186128926 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we have\n\n$$\nR = R_1 \\cup R_2\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nR_1= (0,2) \\times (-1,0)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nR_2= (0,2) \\times (0,1)\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\iint\\limits_{R} f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A &= \\iint\\limits_{R_1} 2 \\ \\textrm d A + \\iint\\limits_{R_2} \\dfrac{1}{xy+x+y+1} \\ \\textrm d A \\\\[5pt] &= 2\\iint\\limits_{R_1} \\textrm d A + \\iint\\limits_{R_2} \\dfrac{1}{(x+1)(y+1)} \\ \\textrm d A \\\\[5pt] &= 2(2-0)(0-(-1)) + \\Bigg(\\int_0^2 \\dfrac{1}{x+1} \\ \\textrm d x \\Bigg) \\Bigg(\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{1}{y+1}\\ \\textrm d y \\Bigg) \\\\[5pt] &= 4 + \\Big[\\ln(x+1)\\Big]_0^2 \\cdot \\Big[\\ln(y+1)\\Big]_0^1 \\\\[5pt] &= 4+ \\ln 3\\ln 2. \\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186128487 17592186128488 17592186128489 17592186128490 17592186128491 17592186128655 17592186128656 17592186128657 17592186128658 17592186128659] "immutable_fields" [[17592186128486 :answer-field/correct] [17592186128486 :answer-field/id] [17592186128486 :answer-field/key] [17592186128486 :answer-field/type] [17592186128654 :answer-field/correct] [17592186128654 :answer-field/id] [17592186128654 :answer-field/key] [17592186128654 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
